 +-------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+-------------+-------------+

+``particles.redistribute_uniform_tile_leave`` is a separate opt-in Boolean
+parameter (default ``false``). It sends every particle through the
+Redistribute leave/pack path, avoiding the GPU stay-count device-to-host
+readback at the cost of packing and buffering 100 percent of local particles.
+If ``N`` particles carry ``S`` packed bytes each, the source tiles and full
+send buffer coexist. In ``D`` dimensions, the GPU path also keeps
+``16 + 4*D`` bytes of ``ParticleCopyOp`` metadata and a 4-byte destination
+index per moved particle, for ``M = 20 + 4*D`` bytes. The pack peak is
+therefore ``2*N*S + N*M``.
+On the shipping NOMPI Metal build, the non-GPU-aware, unpinned send-buffer
+branch also creates a full ``pinned_snd_buffer`` staging copy. Both send
+buffers remain live while destination tiles grow. Thus ``3*N*S + N*M`` is a
+conservative capacity-and-lifetime upper bound; allocator reuse and effective
+buffer capacities can lower the observed high-water mark. For
+``N = 1,048,576`` and ``S = 80 B``, the validated 2D build has ``M = 28 B``:
+upper bounds of 188 MiB at pack and 268 MiB at unpack. The normal estimate is
+80 MiB of payload plus ``(1/128)*80 MiB = 0.625 MiB`` of crossings, or
+80.625 MiB total. The 1M-particle validation measured 152 MiB arena plus
+52 MiB pinned, about 204 MiB host-visible, so it did not reach the bound.
+Conservative 3D sizing adds one 8 B real to the payload: ``S = 88 B`` and
+``M = 32 B`` give 208 MiB at pack and 296 MiB at unpack. The old 160 MiB
+figure was only a payload lower bound. No OOM was observed at 1M; larger cases
+retain OOM risk.
+The mode changes in-tile ordering, so flag-ON versus flag-OFF requires
+order-insensitive particle comparisons and tolerance-based physics checks, not
+bitwise hashes. Enablement aborts with more than one MPI rank. Non-GPU
+single-rank runs exercise host-side semantics only and emit a warning.
+CUDA/HIP runs execute the GPU partition mechanism but remain outside the
+validated backend; they also warn. Mechanism/durability validation covers
+SYCL/Metal; field-level flag-ON evidence remains pending.
+
 The next set concerns runtime parameters that control particle I/O. Parallel file systems tend not to like it when
