+.. py:data:: particles.redistribute_uniform_tile_leave
+   :type: bool
+   :value: false
+
+   This opt-in mode treats every particle in a tile as leaving during
+   :cpp:`ParticleContainer::Redistribute`, then reconstructs particles at their
+   assigned destinations. It avoids the GPU stay-count device-to-host readback,
+   but increases local packing and buffering from roughly the crossing fraction
+   to 100 percent of particles. In ``D`` dimensions, four ``int`` vectors plus
+   a D-int ``IntVect`` give ``16 + 4*D B`` of ``ParticleCopyOp`` metadata;
+   the destination index adds 4 B, so ``M = 20 + 4*D B`` per moved particle.
+   Source payload,
+   the full send buffer, and metadata produce a ``2*N*S + N*M`` pack peak. The
+   shipping NOMPI Metal build then makes a full ``pinned_snd_buffer`` staging
+   copy; both send buffers stay live while destination tiles grow. Thus
+   ``3*N*S + N*M`` is a conservative capacity-and-lifetime upper bound;
+   allocator reuse and effective buffer capacities can lower the observed
+   high-water mark. With ``N = 1,048,576`` and ``S = 80 B``, the validated 2D
+   build has ``M = 28 B``: upper bounds of 188 MiB at pack and 268 MiB at
+   unpack. The normal estimate is 80 MiB of payload plus
+   ``(1/128)*80 MiB = 0.625 MiB`` of crossings, or 80.625 MiB total. The
+   1M-particle validation measured 152 MiB arena plus 52 MiB pinned, about
+   204 MiB host-visible, so it did not reach the bound. Conservative 3D sizing
+   adds one 8 B real to the payload: ``S = 88 B`` and ``M = 32 B`` give
+   208 MiB at pack and 296 MiB at unpack. The former 160 MiB value was only a
+   payload lower bound. No OOM was observed at 1M; larger cases retain OOM
+   risk.
+
+   Flag-ON drains and re-appends particles, changing in-tile ordering relative
+   to flag-OFF. Use order-insensitive particle identity/destination comparisons
+   and tolerance-based physics observables; bitwise/hash equality is invalid.
+   Enablement aborts with more than one MPI rank because that path is
+   unvalidated. Non-GPU runs exercise host-side semantics only and warn.
+   CUDA/HIP runs execute the GPU partition mechanism but warn because the
+   validated backend is SYCL/Metal. Field-level flag-ON evidence remains
+   pending.
+
