+        /*
+         * Uniform full-tile leave on Metal retains the normal
+         * normalize/locate/fallback kernel and its data-dependent stay store,
+         * but makes the relocation shape uniform by treating the whole tile
+         * as leavers. Normal
+         * Redistribute packs roughly f_crossing*N particles; this packs N, so
+         * the volume rises from the crossing fraction to 100% (a
+         * 1/f_crossing multiplier, measured as 128x for 8192/1048576
+         * crossings). The benefit is eliminating the device-to-host
+         * stay-count reduction/readback. The reference micro-harness measured
+         * 39 ms/iteration versus 56 ms for mixed leave/stay at 1M particles
+         * and 64 boxes. The production SYCL/Metal path subsequently completed
+         * a 2000-iteration flag-ON soak and three short WarpX runs; field-level
+         * flag-ON parity remains unvalidated.
+         *
+         * Peak memory follows the Redistribute_impl allocation lifetime. Let
+         * N be the source-particle count and S the packed bytes per particle.
+         * The GPU arm allocates four DeviceVector<int> fields plus one
+         * DeviceVector<IntVect> in ParticleCopyOp: 16 + 4*D B in D
+         * dimensions. ParticleCopyPlan::m_dst_indices adds 4 B, so
+         * M = 20 + 4*D B of move-scaled metadata per particle (28 B in 2D,
+         * 32 B in 3D).
+         *
+         * At packBuffer, source tiles N*S, snd_buffer N*S, and metadata N*M
+         * coexist: 2*N*S + N*M. On the shipping NOMPI Metal configuration,
+         * UseGpuAwareMpi() is false and The_Arena() is not pinned, so the
+         * pinned_snd_buffer branch makes another full N*S staging copy.
+         * snd_buffer and pinned_snd_buffer remain live while unpackBuffer
+         * grows destination tiles to N*S. Thus 3*N*S + N*M is a conservative
+         * capacity-and-lifetime upper bound, excluding allocator/reallocation
+         * overhead; allocator reuse and effective buffer capacities can lower
+         * the observed high-water mark.
+         *
+         * In the validated double-precision hybrid deck, S = 8 B idcpu +
+         * 7*8 B reals + 4*4 B ints = 80 B. At N = 1,048,576, N*S =
+         * 83,886,080 B = 80 MiB. The validated 2D build has M = 28 B,
+         * N*M = 28 MiB, a 188 MiB pack upper bound, and a 268 MiB unpack
+         * upper bound (about 3.3x the normal estimate:
+         * 80 MiB payload + (1/128)*80 MiB crossings = 80.625 MiB).
+         * The 1M-particle validation measured 152 MiB arena plus 52 MiB
+         * pinned, about 204 MiB host-visible, so it did not reach that bound.
+         * Conservative 3D sizing adds one 8 B real to the payload: S = 88 B
+         * and M = 32 B give 208 MiB at pack and 296 MiB at unpack. The former
+         * 160 MiB figure was only the 2*N*S payload lower bound. No OOM was
+         * observed at 1M; that does not guarantee larger configurations.
